# {ProjectName} — Web-Novel Writing Toolkit (OpenClaw)

This project has the OpenClaw compatibility layer of the oh-story skills deployed.

## Skill Routing Table

OpenClaw discovers `SKILL.md` from the project's `skills/` directory. Prefer invoking through OpenClaw's skills/slash-command entry points; if the current client does not show a direct command, name the skill in natural language.

| Command / intent | Skill | Description |
|------|-------|------|
| `/skill story-long-write`, write long-form | story-long-write | Long-form web-novel writing (chapter by chapter) |
| `/skill story-short-write`, write short-form | story-short-write | Short-form web-novel writing (emotion-driven) |
| `/skill story-long-analyze`, long-form teardown | story-long-analyze | Deep teardown of a long-form novel |
| `/skill story-short-analyze`, short-form teardown | story-short-analyze | Teardown analysis of a short-form novel |
| `/skill story-long-scan`, long-form market scan | story-long-scan | Long-form novel rankings and market trends |
| `/skill story-short-scan`, short-form market scan | story-short-scan | Short-form novel rankings and emotional windows |
| `/skill story-deslop`, de-AI-flavor | story-deslop | Removes AI writing traces |
| `/skill story-cover`, cover | story-cover | Generates cover images; requires `GPT_IMAGE_API_KEY` |
| `/skill story-review`, review | story-review | Multi-perspective review; OpenClaw Phase 1 defaults to solo/soft-fallback |
| `/skill story-import`, import | story-import | Reverse-imports an existing novel into the project structure |
| `/skill story`, web novels | story | Toolkit router · auto-routes ambiguous intent |
| `/skill story-setup`, prepare to write a book | story-setup | Environment deployment · multi-CLI configuration entry point |
| `/skill browser-cdp` | browser-cdp | Browser CDP tool |

## OpenClaw Compatibility Notes

- Phase 1 deploys skills only: `skills/*/SKILL.md` uses OpenClaw-compatible frontmatter (`name` / `description` as single-line key-values, `metadata` as single-line JSON).
- OpenClaw agents/hooks are not deployed yet: the pre-prose outline guard, commit reminders, and session/compact auto-injection are not hard interception under OpenClaw; they run as soft constraints inside the skills.
- OpenClaw snapshots eligible skills at session start; if they do not appear immediately after deployment or update, start a new OpenClaw session, or wait for the skills watcher to refresh.
- `story-cover` depends on `GPT_IMAGE_API_KEY`; when it is not configured, OpenClaw marks the skill as unavailable/missing env.

## File Structure

- `skills/` — OpenClaw workspace skills, including oh-story's 13 skills
- `teardown-lib/` — teardown analysis output directory
- `{BookTitle}/prose/` — long-form novel prose chapters
- `{BookTitle}/prose.md` — short-form novel prose
- `{BookTitle}/setting/` — character settings, world settings
- `{BookTitle}/outline/` — volume outlines, chapter outlines
- `{BookTitle}/tracking/` — context.md, foreshadowing.md, timeline.md, character-state.md
- `{BookTitle}/benchmark/` — benchmark-book analysis

## Writing Constraints

- A matching outline must exist before prose is written: long-form `outline/outline_chapter_N*.md`, short-form `section-outline.md`.
- OpenClaw Phase 1 has no hard hook interception; the skill flow itself must check the outline when running a writing skill and must not skip it.
- **Deslop self-lock** (this platform has no hook fallback, so this is the only line of defense): after each chapter's prose is written, within the same turn immediately self-check and clear it using the writing skill's "most toxic sentence patterns quick reference + banned words scan" (run `check-ai-patterns.js --check --fail-on=blocking` when node is available); before writing the next chapter, re-check that the previous chapter has no outstanding debt. The only exemption is the user explicitly saying "don't deslop this chapter"; exempt chapters add `<!-- deslop:skip -->` under the title line.
- After a compact / new session, first read `{BookTitle}/tracking/context.md` to restore current writing progress.

## Restoring Context After Compact

Key writing context:
1. Current writing project name and progress
2. Recently discussed character-setting changes
3. List of unresolved foreshadowing
4. The current chapter's emotion/rhythm targets

If `{BookTitle}/tracking/context.md` exists, read it first after a compact to restore context.
